      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first business was a tannery by Joseph Stutman, and the first house appeared in 1842 built by Charles Stewart.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lewis%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lewis grew into a canal town, with a log schoolhouse serving the community for many years.",
